  "chapter": 637,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 23 Chapter 637\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2258-B, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibit-\n        ing the unauthorized installation of certain security devices on\n        residential buildings\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would prohibit the installation of keyless security  devices\nby  third  parties on residential building entrances without the written\nconsent of the building's ownership or management. This would ensure  no\nentity  can install a device granting access to residential common areas\nwithout the approval of the building owner or manager.\n \n  I support the goals of this legislation, which would protect both  the\nbuilding  owners  and  residents  from entities having unauthorized free\naccess to the building. However, to ensure that residents are also aware\nof the building owner or management granting  third  parties  access  to\ncommon areas, buildings should be required to give notice either direct-\nly  to  residents  or  via  conspicuous  public  notice. If the building\nalready has procedures for tenant notice in its certificate of  incorpo-\nration or by-laws, the building may provide notice by those means. Addi-\ntionally, the legislation should clarify that installation of the device\nis  neither  a  service  to the residents nor a basis to increase rents.\nFinally, the installation of the  device  should  in  no  way  adversely\nimpact or obstruct residents' access to the building.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                           (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                 ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
